# StreamVersion 1.2
# --force-reader names a reader that does not exist, so the file is turned away and a message
# offers "Clear forced reader". Resetting the option alone left the viewport empty: it only acts on
# load, and the load it spoiled had already run. Clicking the action has to load the model again,
# framed as any load frames it (reload_current_file_group keeps the camera it finds, here the empty
# scene's, which showed a close-up of the model's side), and on screen (PRESENTED).
RenderEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
TimerEvent 0 0 0 0 0 0 0
# Click "Clear forced reader" on the message
